  "answer": "Both files are correct. Let me do a final review of the complete solution.\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the route resolution in the request entry point. Two files were edited:\n\n### `entry.mjs` (the production entry point)\n**Before:** `dispatch` called `legacyResolve(path)` first and fell back to the registry. This leaked the legacy `/old/help` compatibility behavior into the production entry point.\n\n**After:** `dispatch(path)` delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`. The legacy API is no longer consulted by the production entry point.\n\n### `registry.mjs` (the lower-level resolver)\n**Before:** It iterated records in declaration order and returned the first match, so the dynamic `/users/:id` shadowed the static `/users/new`, and a fallback encountered early would short-circuit later statics.\n\n**After:** It now implements the required matching policy:\n- Validates `path` (throws `TypeError` for non-strings, empty strings, or paths not starting with `/`).\n- Collects the **first** matching static record, the **first** matching dynamic record, and the **first** fallback independently.\n- Returns priority: **static → dynamic → fallback → `null`**, so any static wins over any dynamic regardless of declaration order, the first matching dynamic wins otherwise, and fallback is used only when neither matched.\n- Never mutates `records`; each call builds fresh result objects and `params` objects, so returned values are independent of later calls.\n\n### Unchanged (as required)\n- `legacy.mjs` — `legacyResolve` and its `/old/help` behavior are untouched.\n- `routes/static.mjs`, `routes/dynamic.mjs`, `routes/fallback.mjs` — already correct (exact/case-sensitive static matching; dynamic matching requires equal segment counts, nonempty dynamic segments, and exact literal segments).\n- `fixtures/routes.mjs`, adapters (`http.mjs`, `cli.mjs`), and utilities (`path.mjs`, `query.mjs`, `headers.mjs`) — left as-is; they continue to behave per their exported APIs.\n\n### Verification against the spec\n- `dispatch('/users/new')` → `{ route: 'user-new', params: {} }` (static beats earlier dynamic).\n- `dispatch('/users/Ada')` → `{ route: 'user-detail', params: { id: 'Ada' } }`.\n- `dispatch('/missing')` → `{ route: 'not-found', params: {} }` (fallback last).\n- `routeHttp('/health?q=one').match` → `{ route: 'health', params: {} }`.\n- `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` → `null`.\n- Invalid inputs (`123`, `''`, `'users'`) throw `TypeError`; trailing slash and case differences do not match.",
